DejaVu LGC Sans (Regular, Bold)
================================

Used by app/services/pdf.py so the case-export PDF can print any Latin,
Greek or Cyrillic text a whistleblower or handler wrote — not just the
latin-1 subset Helvetica (fpdf2's core font) supports. CJK and right-to-left
scripts (Arabic, Hebrew) are outside this font's coverage and are not
supported; see DESIGN.md ("Printed case record") and docs/docs.html.

Source
------

Upstream project: https://github.com/dejavu-fonts/dejavu-fonts
Release:          version_2_37 (2016-07-30)
Archive fetched:  https://github.com/dejavu-fonts/dejavu-fonts/releases/download/version_2_37/dejavu-lgc-fonts-ttf-2.37.zip
                  sha256 bc73bd1c64299a95951fd8c1d493d391ded78cef5b9d3dd3df5859e1f85f5ec6

The GitHub release does not publish an official checksum for this asset
(its API "digest" field is null — the asset predates GitHub's checksum
support). The sha256 above was computed locally right after downloading it
over HTTPS from the URL above; re-download and compare against it, or
against upstream's own build of 2.37, to confirm nothing changed in transit.

Files taken from the archive's ttf/ directory, unmodified:

  DejaVuLGCSans.ttf       sha256 321487efd1b5fa5bffc0597755708fb7b308b3a9a613cebaa013f6a9dd873ab8
  DejaVuLGCSans-Bold.ttf  sha256 0746f87aafab1227658d304e36dab999bfa95f2a6811a1031ca38ed243540a78

"LGC" (Latin/Greek/Cyrillic) is the official subset of the full DejaVu Sans
family, ~1.2 MB for the two weights used here versus ~1.5 MB for the full
family plus Armenian/Georgian/Hebrew glyphs this project makes no claim to
render correctly (no right-to-left shaping) — the smaller, script-scoped
font makes the documented coverage claim (Latin, Greek, Cyrillic) true by
construction rather than by omission.

